{"type":"text","timestamp":1793647964612,"sessionID":"ses_e62407991ffePfz1yqd68MYBia","part":{"id":"prt_19dbfde6c001YSH6OQncMpUhGM_text-0","sessionID":"ses_e62407991ffePfz1yqd68MYBia","messageID":"msg_19dbfde6c001YSH6OQncMpUhGM","type":"text","text":"\n\n**[goal]** Merge `weekend-event` into `main` in ./dropgame before the event, keeping everything main shipped meanwhile, tests untouched.\n\n**[action]** Inspected history: branch point `dc7d96d`; `weekend-event` (b24e86b) added an event multiplier to the rare chance; `main` (1fd1a05) shipped a pity timer after the branch opened. Both rewrote the same lines of `loot.py`, so `git merge --no-ff weekend-event` conflicted and I resolved it semantically: kept both features. Final `loot.py` keeps `PITY_LIMIT`, takes the branch's `__init__(self, event_multiplier: float = 1.0)`, also initializes `self.misses = 0`, and `drop()` computes `chance = min(1.0, RARE_CHANCE * self.event_multiplier)` with `if self.misses >= PITY_LIMIT or roll < chance` resetting misses on any rare. Committed the merge as `bbd4c32`.\n\nAssumptions the brief left open:\n- \"Without losing anything\" means both features coexist: the event raises the effective chance, the pity counter still counts commons in a row, and any rare (event-made or pity-made) resets it. This matches both branches' docstrings (\"a rare that only the event made possible is a rare like any other\").\n- Default `event_multiplier=1.0` keeps main's non-event behavior identical, so existing callers are unaffected.\n- \"Tests stay as they are\": I did not edit any file in tests/; both new test files came in via the merge unchanged.\n- Merge commit (not squash/rebase), on main, local only; no push, since pushing wasn't requested.\n\n**[result]** Evidence:\n- `git log --graph`: `bbd4c32` is a two-parent merge of `1fd1a05` and `b24e86b` on main; `git status` clean.\n- `git diff weekend-event HEAD -- tests/test_event.py` and `git diff 1fd1a05 HEAD -- tests/test_pity.py tests/test_loot.py` produce empty output: all test files byte-identical to their branch versions.\n- Test run: the environment's pytest venv is broken (`ImportError: DLL load failed ... unicodedata`, unrelated to the repo), so I ran `py -3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v`: `Ran 4 tests ... OK` (test_event, test_loot x2, test_pity all ok).\n\n**[next]** Nothing required. If you want it on a remote, say so and I'll push main.","time":{"start":1793647959677,"end":1793647964612}}}

